@title pertisk-eproxy
@copyright 2026 Pertisk
@doc

<h3>Overview</h3>

<p><b>pertisk-eproxy</b> is an Erlang/OTP reverse proxy and Kubernetes ingress
controller built on Cowboy. It terminates HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 (TLS), and optional
HTTP/3 (QUIC), proxies to upstream backends via Gun, and exposes a management
listener (REST API + admin SPA) on port 9080.</p>

<h3>Modes</h3>

<ul>
  <li><b>proxy</b> — sites and backends from SQLite; full read/write admin API.</li>
  <li><b>ingress</b> — routes from Kubernetes standard Ingress resources
      and TLS Secrets; management API is read-only.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Module map</h3>

<ul>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_app} — application start, listener bootstrap.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_handler} — TCP/TLS Cowboy reverse proxy handler.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_h3_api_gateway} — HTTP/3 edge listener and routing.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_config} — runtime configuration (SQLite or ingress JSON).</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_admin_handler} — management REST API.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_ingress_watcher} — Kubernetes Ingress + Secret watcher.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_ingress_reconciler} — Ingress → internal sites/backends transform.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_metrics} — Prometheus counters and histograms.</li>
  <li>{@link pertisk_eproxy_upstream_pool} — shared Gun connection pool.</li>
</ul>

<p>Build HTML API reference: <c>make docs</c> (output in <c>doc/</c>).</p>

<p>Operational guides: repository <c>README.md</c>, <c>README_SQLITE.md</c>,
<c>deploy/helm/pertisk-eproxy/README.md</c>.</p>
